Description: vf_inlineass: make the burned-bitmap (PGS) clear sticky
 refresh_bitmap() recomputes have_bmp every frame from the last uploaded
 bitmap's [bmp_start_ms, bmp_end_ms) window. PGS cues carry
 end_display_time=0, so bmp_end_ms stays -1 and the window is open-ended.
 .
 An empty presentation segment (num_rects==0) sets bmp_pending_clear, and the
 clear frame correctly drops have_bmp and returns early -- but it never closes
 the window. So the VERY NEXT frame skips the pending block and re-runs
 have_bmp = (time_ms >= bmp_start_ms) && (bmp_end_ms < 0 || time_ms < bmp_end_ms)
 = true: the cue resurrects one frame after the clear and hangs on screen until
 the next cue replaces the window. (Found live 2026-05-26: a burned PGS cue
 stayed up until the following cue appeared.)
 .
 Fix: on clear, set bmp_end_ms = time_ms so the per-frame recompute yields
 have_bmp=false until a new bitmap's do_upload resets the window.
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-05-26

--- a/libavfilter/vf_inlineass.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_inlineass.c
@@ -1180,6 +1180,12 @@ static int refresh_bitmap(AVFilterContext *avctx, int64_t time_ms)
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&inlineass_lock);

     if (clear) {
+        /* scaleplex: close the display window so the per-frame have_bmp
+         * recompute below cannot resurrect the cue. PGS cues carry
+         * end_display_time=0 -> bmp_end_ms stays -1; without this the frame
+         * after the clear re-sets have_bmp=(time>=start && end<0)=true and the
+         * cue hangs on screen until the next cue. */
+        ass->bmp_end_ms = time_ms;
         ass->have_bmp = 0;
         return 0;
     }
